From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:46:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: write hud element booleans as an int

HudElem_SetBoolean() stored the value through a VariableUnion pointer.
The field it sets ("archived") is an int. The union is four bytes on
Win32, so nothing changes there, but it holds pointers and is eight
bytes in a 64-bit build, where the write would run into the next field.
---
 src/game/g_hudelem.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/game/g_hudelem.cpp b/src/game/g_hudelem.cpp
index c6f10721..e7962c59 100644
--- a/src/game/g_hudelem.cpp
+++ b/src/game/g_hudelem.cpp
@@ -301,7 +301,7 @@ void __cdecl HudElem_GetFlagHideWhenInMenu(game_hudelem_s *hud, int32_t offset)
 
 void __cdecl HudElem_SetBoolean(game_hudelem_s *hud, int32_t offset)
 {
-    *(VariableUnion *)((char *)&hud->elem.type + fields_0[offset].ofs) = Scr_GetInt(0);
+    *(int32_t *)((char *)&hud->elem.type + fields_0[offset].ofs) = Scr_GetInt(0);
 }
 
 void __cdecl HudElem_SetColor(game_hudelem_s *hud, int32_t offset)
